                    Design: I propose to weight each                            
                    training sample inversely proportional                      
                    to its skin‐tone group frequency, so                        
                    that underrepresented skin tones                            
                    contribute more to the loss and the                         
                    model learns more fairly across tones.                      
                    We compute a `sample_weight` for each                       
                    image as `1/freq(skin_tone)` normalized                     
                    to mean 1, store it in the dataset, and                     
                    use                                                         
                    `BCEWithLogitsLoss(reduction='none')`                       
                    to apply these weights per sample in                        
                    both cross‐validation and full‐data                         
